The opt-in verifier option --bitvector-map-keys also keeps the bitvector type of a multiset element at a multiplicity lookup `ms[k]`, as updates, displays and membership already do, so that `ms[k := n][k] == n` and `multiset{k}[k] == 1` verify for bitvector elements.  With the option on, `m[k := v][k] == v` verifies for maps and imaps with bitvector keys of every width (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/192); with it off, as by default, verification is unchanged.
